From: AX6 EDMA correctness audit
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] edma_v1: fix headroom/tailroom check in TX path

The original code checks skb_headroom(skb) < ntail where ntail is the
needed tailroom. The correct API for tailroom is skb_tailroom().
skb_headroom() returns the space before skb->data, which is unrelated
to the tailroom requirement.

If needed_tailroom is 0 (the common case for EDMA v1 which only sends
head fragments), this bug is dormant. The fix is still required for
correctness and to prevent silent buffer overflow if tailroom is ever
needed (e.g. for L2 header push in VLAN/QinQ configurations).

Fixes F4 from AX6 cross-audit 2026-07-26.
⚠ PATCH NEEDS BUILD-TREE VERIFICATION: confirm the variable name
  (ntail / needed_tailroom) and the exact location in edma_tx_rx.c.

--- a/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_tx_rx.c
+++ b/hal/dp_ops/edma_dp/edma_v1/edma_tx_rx.c
@@ -XXX,XX +XXX,XX @@ static int edma_tx_linearize_or_clone(st

 	if (skb_cloned(skb) ||
 	    skb_headroom(skb) < nhead ||
-	    skb_headroom(skb) < ntail)
+	    skb_tailroom(skb) < ntail)
 		return -ENOMEM;

 	return 0;
